# Community board (자유게시판) — design & API

The community board lets any signed-in regular user of the 수리수리 (MyoDoc) app post threads, comment on other threads, reply to comments, and like posts/comments. It's deliberately scoped narrow — no DMs, no images (v1), no follow graph. The intent is "Naver-cafe-style 게시판" alongside the clinical viewer, not a general social network.

## Data model

```
community_post (id, user_id, title, body, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at)
community_comment (id, post_id, user_id, parent_comment_id?, body, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at)
community_post_like     (user_id, post_id)         -- composite PK
community_comment_like  (user_id, comment_id)      -- composite PK
```

- **Soft delete.** Posts and comments set `deleted_at` instead of being removed. Threads stay navigable; the UI shows a "(deleted)" placeholder.
- **Reply depth = 1.** A comment with `parent_comment_id` is a reply. A reply to a reply is *flattened* server-side — its `parent_comment_id` is rewritten to the top-level comment so the tree never goes deeper than one level. This matches Naver/Kakao 카페 conventions and keeps rendering simple.
- **Likes are idempotent.** The composite primary key makes the second `POST /like` a P2002, which the route swallows. Both POST and DELETE always return the *current* `likeCount`.

## Endpoints (all under `/api/mobile/community`)

| Method | Path | Auth | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| GET | `/posts?cursor=&pageSize=` | ✅ | Reverse-chrono list with keyset pagination |
| POST | `/posts` | ✅ | Create a new post (`title`, `body`) |
| GET | `/posts/:id` | ✅ | Full post with `commentCount`, `likeCount`, `likedByMe` |
| PATCH | `/posts/:id` | ✅ (author) | Edit `title` and/or `body` |
| DELETE | `/posts/:id` | ✅ (author) | Soft-delete |
| GET | `/posts/:id/comments` | ✅ | Flat list, newest at bottom — client builds the tree |
| POST | `/posts/:id/comments` | ✅ | Comment or reply (`body`, `parentCommentId?`) |
| DELETE | `/comments/:id` | ✅ (author) | Soft-delete |
| POST | `/posts/:id/like` | ✅ | Idempotent like; returns `{ liked, likeCount }` |
| DELETE | `/posts/:id/like` | ✅ | Idempotent unlike |
| POST | `/comments/:id/like` | ✅ | Idempotent like on a comment |
| DELETE | `/comments/:id/like` | ✅ | Idempotent unlike |

### List response example

```json
{
  "posts": [
    {
      "id": "uuid",
      "title": "아토핀 0.05% 사용 후기",
      "bodyPreview": "저희 아이는 작년 3월부터…",
      "author": { "id": "uuid", "username": "alice", "isMe": false },
      "createdAt": "2026-05-14T03:21:00Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-05-14T03:21:00Z",
      "commentCount": 12,
      "likeCount": 4,
      "likedByMe": true
    }
  ],
  "nextCursor": "uuid-of-last-post"
}
```

### Comment payload

```json
{
  "id": "uuid",
  "postId": "uuid",
  "parentCommentId": null,
  "body": "저도 6개월째 쓰는데…",
  "deleted": false,
  "author": { "id": "uuid", "username": "bob", "isMe": false },
  "createdAt": "2026-05-14T03:25:00Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-05-14T03:25:00Z",
  "likeCount": 1,
  "likedByMe": false
}
```

When a comment is soft-deleted, `body` is `null` and `deleted` is `true`. The author/timestamps are preserved so reply attribution still makes sense.

## Moderation hooks (out of scope for v1)

The schema reserves `deleted_at` as the moderation point of control. A future `/admin/community/*` route (web-side, `loginRequired` + `siteAdminRequired`) can set `deleted_at` on any post/comment. No table changes needed.
